{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1759019,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":"blue_un","paid":0,"title":"IMI MUN 2026","festival_id":null,"organization_id":553,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-09-25T00:00:08+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-25T17:00:05+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/imi-mun-2026-international-management-institute-imi-new-delhi-1759019","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>Event Overview:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>The Internationalization Committee of the International Management Institute, Delhi is hosting the Model United Nations on 24th and 25th October, 2026. Over two days, students will take on the role of delegates and will debate, negotiate and work out solutions to pressing global challenges.<\/p>\n<p>MUN is an academic simulation of the United Nations, where delegates represent countries, organisations and political voices and approach real-world issues from the point of view of their assigned portfolio. It is a place to practice diplomacy, sharpen your thinking and understand the world better.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Registration Details:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Registration fee: \u20b9799 per delegate<\/li>\n<li>Dates: 24th and 25th October, 2026<\/li>\n<li>Timing: 9:00 AM to 5:00 PM<\/li>\n<li>Venue: IMI Delhi<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Cash Prizes:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Best Delegate: UNSC - \u20b915,000 | AIPPM - \u20b915,000 | G20 - \u20b915,000<\/li>\n<li>Outstanding Delegate: UNSC - \u20b911,000 | AIPPM - \u20b911,000 | G20 - \u20b911,000<\/li>\n<li>Special Mention: UNSC - \u20b92,000 | AIPPM - \u20b92,000 | G20 - \u20b92,000 | (3 delegates per committee)<\/li>\n<li>Best International Press: \u20b92,000 | (Best 2 out of 6 members)<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Exciting Perks for Delegates:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cash prizes: 1 lakh prize pool along with other rewards.<\/li>\n<li>Certificates: Every delegate receives one.<\/li>\n<li>Goodies basket: Gifts for all participants.<\/li>\n<li>Meals: Food is provided for both days.<\/li>\n<li>Trophies: Awards for the top 2 performers across different categories.<\/li>\n<li>Networking: A chance to meet and build lasting connections with people who love global affairs and diplomacy as much as you do.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Theme:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>The Game of Nations:<\/strong> Access to education, the effectiveness of the Security Council, and the dominance of the dollar are all shifting, and each reflects the same tension between national self-interest and collective stability. This year's theme asks delegates to think about what rules should replace the old arrangements as they weaken.<\/p>\n<p><strong>Committees and Agendas:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>All India Political Parties Meet (AIPPM):<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Agenda: The Right to Learn, The Fight for a Seat<\/p>\n<p>Access to education has become one of the most contested issues in India, with millions of students competing for a limited number of seats. Delegates will debate reservation and merit, the cost of coaching and private education, the rural-urban and digital divide, and how well the Right to Education works in practice.<\/p>\n<p><strong>United Nations Security Council (UNSC):<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Agenda: The Middle East Crisis: Veto Power and UNSC Effectiveness<\/p>\n<p>Repeated use of the veto by permanent members has left the Council divided on the Middle East crisis and raised questions about its relevance. Delegates will discuss whether the veto should be reformed, how to balance humanitarian access with state sovereignty, and whether expanding the Council can restore its credibility.<\/p>\n<p><strong>G20:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Agenda: De-dollarisation: A New Global Financial Order or a New Global Divide?<\/p>\n<p>More economies, especially in BRICS and the Global South, are looking to trade in local currencies and depend less on the US dollar. Delegates will debate whether this leads to a fairer, multipolar financial system or splits the global economy, and what it means for developing countries.<\/p>\n<p><strong>International Press (IP):<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>Press delegates don't debate a fixed agenda. Instead, they take on the role of journalists whose job is to question rather than report, pressing delegates on their statements and holding them accountable for their country's positions throughout the conference.<\/p>\n<p><strong>General Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>IMI Delhi MUN 2026 is a two-day event, running from 24th to 25th October, 2026.<\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Please check the Committee Allocation Matrix before choosing your preferred committee .&nbsp; <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/docs.google.com\/spreadsheets\/d\/1BpLedz88L7GjEuJNyFn108bfen7dyipVxYUfCMfdfqo\/edit?gid=1870133606#gid=1870133606\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Matrix Link<\/span><\/a><\/li>\n<li>Committee and country\/portfolio preferences must be filled in through the application form at the time of registration. The Organizing Committee will make the final allocations.<\/li>\n<li>Registered delegates will get study guides and event details by email before the conference.<\/li>\n<li>The Organizing Committee's decision on allocations is final and binding.<\/li>\n<li>Delegates must follow the Business Formal dress code.<\/li>\n<li>To stay eligible for awards, delegates must attend all committee sessions on both days. Please see the official MUN guidelines for more details.<\/li>\n<li>Decisions made by the Executive Board (EB) and the Organizing Committee are final and binding.<\/li>\n<li>The Organizing Committee may change schedules, agendas or logistics if needed, and will let everyone know as soon as possible.<\/li>\n<li>IMI Delhi may use photos and videos taken during the event for official purposes.<\/li>\n<li>Registration is confirmed only after the fee is paid. Fees are non-refundable if a delegate withdraws.<\/li>\n<li>Please be professional, respectful and courteous throughout the event so that everyone has a good experience. Misconduct or breaking protocol can lead to disqualification.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Get set to debate, decide, and drive change!<\/p>\n<p><strong>Register now to reserve your spot at IMI Delhi MUN 2026.<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>We look forward to seeing you there.<\/strong><\/p>","overall_prizes":"Prizes worth \u20b91,00,000","regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":null,"registration_clicks":0,"user_id":659849,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-09-20T21:12:38+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-05T20:11:50+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competition","combined_leaderboard":null,"source":null,"short_id":"DHuIJnf","hashtags":null,"participation_certificate":1,"winner_certificate_at":null,"listed":1,"self_moderated":2,"prizes_release_days":null,"checked":1,"display_title":null,"show_discussions_only_user":1,"show_reviews_only_user":1,"show_score_card":0,"players_count":14,"referral_leaderboard_show":0,"is_ad_free":0,"enable_gamify_leaderboard":0,"tpo_college_id":null,"publish_at":"2026-09-20 21:12:38","auto_shortlist_trigger":false,"enable_ai_discussion":false,"total_unlock_teams":0,"enable_hiring_automation":false,"auto_send_participation_certificate":false,"closed_at":null,"linkedInEventId":"","teams":[],"players":[],"logoUrl":"https:\/\/d8it4huxumps7.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/images\/75x75\/uploadedManual-6ac26313a94b3_mun_1.png","logoUrl2":"https:\/\/d8it4huxumps7.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/images\/150x150\/uploadedManual-6ac26313a94b3_mun_1.png","regnRequirements":{"id":2490530,"opportunity_id":1759019,"festival_id":null,"max_team_size":1,"min_team_size":1,"start_regn_dt":"2026-09-25T00:00:08+05:30","end_regn_dt":"2026-10-15T23:59:08+05:30","show_deadline":1,"open_for":0,"college_type":0,"same_organisation":0,"study_year_filter":0